1.3  Loss Occurrence
“Loss Occurrence” means all individual losses arising out of and directly occasioned by one catastrophe.
The duration and extent of any Loss Occurrence shall be limited to:
(a) a period of 72 consecutive hours arising out of and directly occasioned by windstorm, tempest, hurricane,
tornado, cyclone or typhoon, including resultant storm surge and rainfall;
(b) a period of 168 consecutive hours arising out of and directly occasioned by flood or inundation not
otherwise excluded;
(c) a period of 72 consecutive hours arising out of and directly occasioned by earthquake, seaquake, volcanic
eruption or subterranean fire;
(d) a period of 168 consecutive hours in respect of riot, civil commotion or malicious damage, provided such
losses arise within the boundaries of one city or town.
The Company may choose the date and time at which any such period commences, provided that no two
periods overlap and that no period commences earlier than the date and time of the first recorded individual
loss.

